(a) No person shall engage in the business of a building contractor in the city unless such person holds a valid unrevoked and unsuspended license as a qualified building contractor issued by the director of inspections.
(b) It shall be unlawful for any building contractor operating within the city or the county as a contractor to permit any one of the following acts or omissions:
(1) To contract to do any work outside the scope of operations as defined under the particular type of contractor for which he is licensed;
(2) To depart from or disregard in any material respect, the plan or specifications of a construction job without approval of the building inspector of the city;
(3) Disregard or violate in the performance of his construction job any of the building code or safety requirements, or health regulations of the city and the county;
(4) Misrepresent any material fact in his application and attendant papers in obtaining a certificate under this article;
(5) Aid or abet an unqualified person to evade provisions of this article, or allow one's certificate to be used by an unqualified person or act as an agent, partner or associate of an unqualified person with an intent to evade the provisions of this article;
(6) Fail to fulfill contractual obligations through failure to pay all creditors for material furnished or work or services performed which result in the successful termination by the courts in favor of the lienholder who files a mechanic's or materialman's lien against the property upon which work was performed in the operation of his business for which he is qualified under this article; or
(7) Abandon without legal excuse, construction projects or operations engaged in or under contract as a contractor.
(Ord. No. 97-36, § 7-1090, 6-5-1997)
